UPDATE companies SET description='Crego Metal Systems, operating as Crego Roofing of New Mexico, has been based in Albuquerque’s North Valley (Los Ranchos de Albuquerque) since its founding in 1980. The company is family‑owned and operated, with Stephen and Brenda Gregg serving as primary contacts. It began as a local installer and manufacturer of metal roofing for both residential and commercial projects.

The firm fabricates cut‑to‑length metal roof panels, flashing, and trim on site using UL‑approved roll‑forming lines. Its product range includes CMS Panel, R Panel, and Standing Seam profiles, along with seamless and box gutters, plaster trims, and plasma‑cut decorative silhouettes. Custom copper work and green‑roof solutions are also offered. Most standard orders are ready for same‑day pickup; larger orders typically ship within three days.

Crego serves homeowners, building owners, and contractors across residential and commercial construction in New Mexico. Its metal roofing and gutter systems are used on houses, office buildings, and retail centers, while its plasma‑cut designs and copper accents appear on custom architectural projects.

The company emphasizes its UL‑approved manufacturing standards and ANSI/SPRI/ES‑1‑tested flashing that exceeds wind‑uplift requirements. A price‑match guarantee and family‑run continuity since 1980 are cited as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['UL approved (roof panel machine lines)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cut-to-length metal roof panel fabrication", "Roof flashing fabrication", "Roll forming (CMS Panel, R Panel, Standing Seam)", "Plasma cutting", "Custom metal design and fabrication", "Seamless gutter fabrication", "Box gutter fabrication", "Custom copper fabrication", "Metal profiling", "Installation services (residential and commercial roofing)"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Roofing", "Green building", "Custom metal fabrication", "Architectural metalwork"], "materials": ["Galvalume", "Copper", "Painted steel (Saddle Tan, Rustic Red)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day pickup for standard orders; 3 days or less for larger orders", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["UL\u2011approved roof panel roll\u2011forming lines", "ANSI/SPRI/ES\u20111 tested flashing exceeding wind\u2011uplift standards", "Same\u2011day pickup for most cut\u2011to\u2011length orders", "Three\u2011day maximum lead time for larger orders", "Family\u2011owned and operated since 1980"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1980 -> db", "Family-owned and operated since 1980 -> /", "Location: Albuquerque, NM (Los Ranchos de Albuquerque) -> /about", "Manufactures cut-to-length metal roof panels and flashing on site -> /about", "UL approved roof panel machine lines -> /about", "ANSI/SPRI/ES-1 tested flashing exceeding wind uplift standards -> /about", "Same-day pickup for most orders; 3 days or less for larger orders -> /about", "Plasma cutting and custom metal design -> /, /about", "Custom copper design and green solutions -> /about", "Seamless and box gutter fabrication -> /, /about", "Price match guarantee -> /", "Contacts: Stephen Gregg, Brenda Gregg -> /about", "Business license #401273, CRS# 03-516317-008 -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a local installer and leading manufacturer of residential and commercial metal roofs since 1980", "founded_year": "1980", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='crego-metal-systems' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Crittco Cable & Fiber operates from Jonesboro, Arkansas, where it was founded in 2002 by Matt Hale and Barry Brawner as a subsidiary of Crittco Construction. Hale brought two decades of water and sewer experience, while Brawner contributed 30 years in telecommunications. The company incorporated in May 2007 and is licensed in Arkansas and Tennessee.

The firm functions as a full‑service utility contractor with directional drilling as its cornerstone. It runs six drill rigs ranging from a 7×11 unit for tight urban sites to a 24×40 rig capable of 28‑inch bores, and can pull back single steel or multiple poly pipes. Additional capabilities include copper and fiber‑optic splicing (single and ribbon), plowing, cable pulling and tugging, trenching and excavating with equipment up to a 200‑series excavator, utility locating, aerial fiber and copper placement, duct washing, fiber blowing, and sewer, water, drainage and electric installation. The operation occupies roughly 8,000 square feet of shop space plus storage and a covered wash bay, supported by a fleet of boring rigs, bucket trucks, backhoes, mini excavators, plows, vacuum excavators, bulldozers, and specialized safety gear. Headcount has grown from the original 12 to around 30 employees.

Crittco serves telecommunications carriers such as Ritter Communications and AT&T, municipal utilities including City Water and Light, and commercial construction projects for Hino Motors, Sam’s Wholesale, Greene County Tech School, and Home Depot. It has also performed infrastructure work around new runways at Memphis International Airport and handles private subdivision and municipal projects in the Marion and West Memphis areas.

