e racks, wire shelving, retail display racks, shelf standards, wall standards, and shelf brackets.", "founded_year": "1948", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='crown-metal-manufacturing-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Custom Cable Corp., based in Westbury, New York, has operated since 1974. What began as a small Long Island distributor has grown into a global supplier of industrial wire and cable.

The firm stocks more than 15,000 active wire and cable variations, ranging from high-temperature and coaxial cables to multi-conductor and fiber-optic products. In addition to distribution, it provides value-added fabrication services including precision striping, twisting, paralleling, bundling with custom printing, dyeing, and lashing. The shop also builds generator cable assemblies and fiber patch cords for high-current and high-speed data applications. A team whose combined experience exceeds 150 years, with sales professionals averaging 25 years in the industry, supports technical consulting and rapid fulfillment programs such as emergency shipments and just-in-time delivery.

Customers span manufacturing, aerospace, construction, electronics, and energy and utilities sectors. Testimonials cite senior engineers, project managers, procurement leads, and plant supervisors from those industries who rely on Custom Cable for both standard stock and custom assemblies. The company also serves OEMs, contractors, and other distributors.

Custom Cable was founded on the principle of supplying wire and cable by specification rather than description, emphasizing knowledgeable service and long-term relationships. Its stated differentiators include deep inventory, seasoned technical support, and a commitment to compliance with standards such as UL, NEMA, ICEA, MIL, CSA, and VW-1.', certifications=ARRAY['ROHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Striping", "Twisting", "Paralleling", "Bundling", "Bundling Custom Printing", "Dyeing", "Lashing", "Generator Cable Assemblies", "Fiber Patch Cords", "Custom Cable Solutions", "Inventory & Rapid Fulfillment", "Technical Support & Consulting", "Quality & Standards Compliance"], "industries": ["Manufacturing", "Aerospace", "Construction", "Electronics", "Energy & Utilities"], "materials": ["Copper", "Aluminum", "Fiber Optic"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["More than 15,000 active wire and cable variations in stock", "Sales professionals average over 25 years of experience", "Combined team expertise exceeding 150 years", "Value-added fabrication: striping, twisting, paralleling, bundling, custom printing, dyeing, lashing", "Custom generator cable assemblies and fiber patch cords"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1974 -> db, /, /about-us", "Headquarters Westbury, New York -> db", "More than 15,000 active wire and cable variations in stock -> /capabilities", "Sales professionals average over 25 years experience -> /capabilities", "Combined team expertise exceeding 150 years -> /capabilities", "Value-added services: striping, twisting, paralleling, bundling, custom printing, dyeing, lashing -> /capabilities", "Generator cable assemblies and fiber patch cords -> /capabilities", "Custom cable solutions for non-standard configurations -> /capabilities", "Inventory & rapid fulfillment: emergency shipments, just-in-time delivery -> /capabilities", "Technical support & consulting -> /capabilities", "Quality & standards compliance: UL, NEMA, ICEA, MIL, CSA, VW-1 -> /capabilities", "Industries served: manufacturing, aerospace, construction, electronics, energy & utilities -> /, /about-us (testimonials)", "Certification: ROHS -> db", "Company type: distributor -> /about-us", "Founded on principle: supply by specification, knowledgeable service, long-term relationships -> /about-us", "Built on Relationships. Driven by Service. -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "What began as a small Long Island distributor has grown into a global supplier; Generator Cable Assemblies and Fiber Patch Cords listed as capabilities", "founded_year": "1974", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='custom-cable-corp' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Custom Cut & Fab operates from Mandan, North Dakota, where its staff has been active in metal fabrication since 1992. The business began with a focus on HVAC fabrication and the general construction trade, building a reputation for evaluating customer drawings and resolving design challenges before production starts.

The shop provides custom metal fabrication services, including HVAC fittings, galvanized and stainless steel components, and copper countertops. Its primary processes are water jet cutting on a 6‑by‑12‑foot table capable of slicing material up to 7 inches thick and as thin as 0.002 inch, and plasma cutting on a 5‑by‑10‑foot table suited for metal up to 3/16 inch thick. The water jet handles a wide range of materials — stone, marble, granite, plastics, foam, wood, and ceramics — while the plasma table is geared toward HVAC parts and metal art pieces.

The company serves the HVAC, general construction, and metal arts sectors. Customers range from contractors needing a subcontractor for specific fabrication tasks to clients who want a single source to manage a project from initial design through final delivery.

What sets the operation apart is its long‑tenured team and its willingness to review drawings early, identify potential issues, and propose work‑arounds. The firm emphasizes taking a client’s vision and delivering a finished project, whether that means supplying a single fitting or coordinating a full fabrication package.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["HVAC fabrication", "Custom metal fabrication", "Water jet cutting", "Plasma cutting", "Drawing evaluation", "Project management", "Galvanized steel fabrication", "Stainless steel fabrication", "Copper countertop fabrication", "Metal arts design"], "industries": ["HVAC", "General construction", "Metal arts"], "materials": ["Galvanized steel", "Stainless steel", "Copper", "Stone", "Marble", "Granite", "Plastic", "Foam", "Wood", "Ceramics"], "equipment": ["Water Jet (6'' x 12'')", "Plasma Table (5'' x 10'')"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Staff experience dating to 1992", "Water jet cutting up to 7\" thick and 0.002\" thin", "Plasma cutting up to 3/16\" thick", "Drawing evaluation and issue resolution", "End\u2011to\u2011end project management"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1992 -> db", "Headquarters Mandan, North Dakota -> db", "Staff in business since 1992, specializing in HVAC fabrication and general construction trade -> /", "Custom metal fabrication company -> /", "Provide expert assistance, subcontractor for metal fabrication, handle projects from beginning to end -> /", "Evaluate drawings and determine what can be done and work around issues -> /", "HVAC fittings fabrication -> /", "Custom fabrication: galvanized, stainless steel, copper countertops -> /", "Special projects -> /", "Water Jet equipment: 6''x12'', cuts up to 7\" thick, .002 material, cuts various materials -> /", "Plasma Table: 5''x10'', cuts up to 3/16\" thick metal, used for HVAC fabrication and Metal Arts Design -> /", "Industries: HVAC, general construction, metal arts design -> /", "Materials: galvanized steel, stainless steel, copper, stone, marble, granite, plastic, foam, wood, ceramics -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a custom metal fabrication company providing customers with expert assistance in completing their project.", "founded_year": "1992", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='custom-cut-and-fab' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1979 in Mobile, Alabama, Custom Metal Fabrication, Inc. (CMFI) began as a metal fabrication shop serving industrial and marine markets.

CMFI provides industrial fabrication, marine fabrication, and engineering design services. Its shop handles carbon steel, stainless steel, and aluminum, offering metal bending, custom fabrication, and prototype-to-renovation work. Marine projects cover commercial and pleasure craft, including interior and exterior fabrication. The engineering team uses AutoCAD, Rhino, Fusion 360, and SOLIDWORKS for surface modeling, solid modeling, piping design, and finite element analysis.

The company serves industrial manufacturers and marine builders, producing components for commercial vessels, pleasure craft, and general industrial applications. Customers range from prototype developers to renovation contractors.

