UPDATE companies SET description='Colorado Springs Sawmill at Penrose operates from Penrose, Colorado, where it transforms locally sourced and imported wood into custom furniture, timber art, and live-edge slabs. The company''s motto—“from disaster to design”—reflects its origins in urban milling, turning trees removed from properties into usable lumber and finished pieces. While the founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed, the business is closely associated with craftsman Mitch, who is highlighted in customer testimonials for his pride in each piece.

The sawmill offers a range of woodworking services including furniture design, timber art, DIY furniture kits, imported live-edge slabs, and fireplace mantels. It also provides urban milling—processing logs on-site or at its facility—and kiln-drying services for hire. Complementing the woodworking side, the company runs arborist services such as technical crane removals and pruning, creating a vertical integration from tree removal to finished product.

Customers include homeowners seeking custom pieces from their own trees, cabin and campground operators needing rustic furnishings, and woodworkers purchasing live-edge slabs for projects. The arborist services cater to residential and commercial property owners in the Colorado Springs region. Testimonials reference homes, cabins, and campgrounds as typical end-use settings.

The company differentiates itself by offering a closed-loop service: clients can have a tree removed, milled, dried, and crafted into furniture all through one provider. This “tree-to-table” approach, combined with the ability to work with a client’s own timber, creates a unique sentimental and sustainable value proposition.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Furniture Design", "Timber Art", "DIY Furniture", "Imported live-Edge Slabs", "Fireplace Mantels", "Arborist Services", "Urban Milling", "Kiln for Hire"], "industries": ["Arboriculture", "Custom furniture manufacturing", "Wood products", "Live-edge slab distribution"], "materials": ["Wood (local and imported)", "Metal", "Live-edge wood slabs"], "equipment": ["Kiln"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Urban milling of local trees into lumber", "Kiln-drying services available for hire", "Integrated arborist and woodworking services", "Custom furniture made from client\u2019s own trees"], "facts_used": ["Location: Penrose, Colorado -> /", "Address: 240 3rd Street, Penrose, CO 81240 -> /", "Phone:  -> /", "Motto: ''from disaster to design'' -> /", "Services: Furniture Design, Timber Art, DIY Furniture, Imported live-Edge Slabs, Fireplace Mantels, Arborist Services, Urban Milling, Kiln for Hire -> /", "Testimonials mention craftsman Mitch and custom pieces for homes, cabins, campgrounds -> /", "Capability: Arborist Services -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Furniture Design, Timber Art, DIY Furniture, Imported live-Edge Slabs, Fireplace Mantels, Arborist Services, Urban Milling, Kiln for Hire", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='custom-woodworking-colorado-springs-sawmill-at-penrose-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Custom Works Inc. operates from Naperville, Illinois, where Serbian‑Macedonian couple Stefan and Melanie founded the company to blend Stefan’s carpentry heritage with Melanie’s project‑management expertise. Stefan grew up in a small town in southern Serbia, spending school holidays in his grandfather Stojan’s workshop, while Melanie brought a background in interior design and operations. Together they launched Custom Works as a vehicle for European‑inspired craftsmanship in the Chicago suburbs.

The shop produces custom furniture, cabinetry, built‑ins, vanities, and one‑off wood pieces, and pairs that output with full‑service home remodeling—kitchens, bathrooms, staircases, mudrooms—and outdoor construction such as patios, decks, and custom exterior features. Projects move through a four‑step design‑build process: consultation, design approval, fabrication (with a typical 8‑10‑week lead time), and on‑site installation.

The client base is residential homeowners across the Chicagoland area. Recent work includes a full basement rebuild after flood damage with a custom bar and media wall, a kitchen remodel that opened up the floor plan and added lighting, a sentimental coffee table milled from a family tree stored for a year, a mudroom with integrated storage, and an entertainment wall with custom TV stand and paneling.

The founders frame the business around four stated values—sustainability, tradition, integrity, and quality—describing their approach as the “European way.” All lumber and materials are said to be ethically and responsibly sourced, and the goal is to create pieces that last for generations rather than follow fast‑furniture trends.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom woodworking", "Cabinetry", "Built-ins", "Vanities", "Custom furniture", "Full home remodeling", "Kitchen remodeling", "Bathroom remodeling", "Staircase construction", "Mudroom construction", "Outdoor construction", "Patio building", "Deck building", "Custom outdoor features", "Design services", "Installation", "Project management"], "industries": ["Residential remodeling", "Custom furniture", "Cabinetry", "Outdoor living"], "materials": ["Wood (ethically sourced)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "8-10 weeks for custom products", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Ethically and responsibly sourced wood and materials", "Furniture designed to last for generations", "European-inspired craftsmanship values (tradition, quality, integrity, sustainability)", "Integrated design-build process with 8-10 week lead time", "Transparent communication throughout project"], "facts_used": ["Location: Naperville, Illinois -> db", "Founders: Stefan (CEO) and Melanie (Co-founder) -> /about", "Founding story: Stefan''s carpentry background in Serbia -> /about", "Services: custom woodworking, cabinetry, full home remodeling, outdoor construction -> /", "Process: 4-step design-build with 8-10 week lead time -> /", "Values: sustainability, tradition, integrity, quality; ethically sourced materials -> /about", "Client examples: basement remodel, kitchen remodel, custom coffee table, mudroom, entertainment wall -> /", "Materials: ethically sourced wood -> /about", "Lead time: 8-10 weeks for delivery -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Custom-designed furniture and cabinetry built specifically for your home.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='custom-works-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Cut & Dry Lumber Company operates an urban sawmill in Albuquerque, New Mexico. The business was launched in 2018 by a family that had spent more than 40 years in the local tree-service industry, during which they consistently diverted tree material from landfills into wood chips and firewood. The sawmill formalized that practice by processing trees removed from the Albuquerque urban forest into usable lumber.

The company produces live-edge slabs typically cut 2 inches thick with the natural edge intact, and offers custom milling, planing, and finishing services on its Wood-Mizer LX 250 band mill (54-inch capacity, 18-foot length), a 24-inch industrial planer, a 16-inch jointer, and a large sander. It also builds made-to-order furnishings such as river tables, bar tops, desks, benches, and charcuterie boards. All lumber is air-dried for up to two years — one year as logs, then six to eight months after milling — to stabilize the wood in the desert climate.

Customers include interior designers, woodworkers, DIY enthusiasts, and anyone seeking custom furniture made from local species. The shop stocks slabs from Ash, Cottonwood, Cypress, Elm, Honey Locust, Juniper, Maple, Mulberry, Pine, Poplar, Russian Olive, and Sycamore, priced between $5 and $22 per board foot. It does not carry kiln-dried, treated, or structural lumber.

The venture was started to expand the tree-recycling culture in New Mexico, turning what would be waste into one-of-a-kind material that preserves a piece of Albuquerque’s urban forest in homes, shops, and gathering spaces.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Live-edge slab production", "Custom milling", "Planing", "Finishing", "Made-to-order furnishings", "Air drying of lumber"], "industries": ["Interior design", "Woodworking", "Furniture manufacturing", "DIY/home improvement", "Custom furnishings"], "materials": ["Ash", "Cottonwood", "Cypress", "Elm", "Honey Locust", "Juniper", "Maple", "Mulberry", "Pine", "Poplar", "Russian Olive", "Sycamore"], "equipment": ["Wood-Mizer LX 250 band mill", "Industrial 24\" planer", "16\" jointer", "Large sander"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% sourced and crafted in Albuquerque from urban-forest trees", "Live-edge slabs cut 2\" thick with natural edge intact", "Custom milling, planing, and finishing on Wood-Mizer LX 250 band mill (54\" x 18\")", "Made-to-order furnishings including river tables, bar tops, and charcuterie boards"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2018 by family with 40+ years in tree service -> /about", "Urban sawmill processing Albuquerque trees -> /about, /", "Equipment: Wood-Mizer LX 250, 24\" planer, 16\" jointer, large sander -> /services", "Species list: Ash, Cottonwood, Cypress, Elm, Honey Locust, Juniper, Maple, Mulberry, Pine, Poplar, Russian Olive, Sycamore -> /services", "Slabs 2\" thick, natural edge, $5-22/bf -> /services", "Air-dry timeline up to 2 years -> /services", "Services: live-edge slabs, custom milling, made-to-order furnishings -> /services", "Customer types: interior designers, woodworkers, DIYers -> /, /services", "Mission: reduce green waste, build tree recycling culture -> /about, /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "we decided to take our efforts to the next level by starting an urban sawm