UPDATE companies SET description='Dickson Industries Inc. traces its roots to April 30, 1946, when Allied Manufacturing Co. was founded at 115 SW 8th Street in Des Moines, Iowa. The company began producing cotton stockinette for meat packers and food processors. Arthur D. Dickson, initially hired as a sales engineer, purchased the business in the 1960s and renamed it Dickson Industries, Inc., moving operations to the Interstate Bakery Building at 325 SW 5th Street. Now in its third generation of family ownership, the company is led by President David Dickson, grandson of the founder.

Today Dickson operates a 50,000-square-foot facility in Des Moines with 49 employees and 216 knitting machines, offering complete cut-and-sew operations and in-house embroidery through its Dickson Designs division. The company produces a range of knit fabrics, garments, and textile products, including custom-designed casings, stockinette, medical fabrics, lab and butcher coats, insulated garments, and filtration fabrics. All products are researched, tested, and manufactured to customer specifications, with proprietary information kept confidential.

Dickson serves food processing (DeliKnit elastic netting, RoastKnit, butcher coats), medical (PPE, surgical drapes, orthopedic fabrics, infant caps, lab coats), industrial (DrainKnit filtration covers, geo textiles, protective sleeves), and apparel markets (custom embroidery, freezerwear, hospitality garments). Its customer base spans national and international businesses, with a centralized Midwest location enabling quick delivery across the United States.

Dickson differentiates itself through collaborative custom product development, emergency response capabilities, and a nationwide sales team that provides ongoing consultation.', certifications=ARRAY['SQF (Safe Quality Foods)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Knit fabric manufacturing", "Cut and sew operations", "Custom textile design", "Embroidery (Dickson Designs)", "Product testing and research", "Confidential product development", "Custom packaging and shipping", "Emergency order fulfillment", "Filtration fabric production", "Medical textile manufacturing", "Food processing garment production", "Geotextile production"], "industries": ["Food Processing", "Medical", "Industrial", "Apparel", "Personal Protective Equipment (PPE)", "Filtration", "Hospitality", "Geotextiles"], "materials": ["Cotton", "Yarn", "Knit fabrics"], "equipment": ["216 knitting machines", "High-tech knitting machines (65 added in 2005)", "Cut and sew equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1946 as Allied Manufacturing Co. -> /about", "Located in Des Moines, Iowa -> /about", "Family-owned, third generation -> /about", "President David Dickson (third generation) -> /about", "49 employees -> /about", "216 knitting machines -> /about", "50,000 sq ft facility -> /about", "SQF certification acquired 2018 -> /about", "Products: knit fabrics, garments, textile products -> /", "Industries: food processing, medical, industrial, apparel -> /", "Custom cut and sew, embroidery -> /about", "DeliKnit, RoastKnit, DrainKnit product lines -> /about", "Centralized Midwest location for quick delivery -> /about", "Confidential product development -> /about", "Emergency response and custom shipping -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Proud producer of quality, innovative knit fabrics, garments, and textile products.", "founded_year": "1946", "employee_count": "49", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "",