UPDATE companies SET description='Dixon Power Systems operates from Lincoln, Nebraska, where Jon and Holly Dixon launched the business in the spring of 1999 after Jon spent 17 years running an automotive repair shop. The venture began part‑time and moved to full‑time operation in January 2005, driven by Jon’s growing interest in renewable energy and Holly’s encouragement.

The company designs and installs solar photovoltaic and wind generation systems for customers seeking energy independence. A storefront allows visitors to learn about and purchase equipment for producing their own electricity. Jon applies his automotive mechanical and electrical background to tailor each system for site‑specific constraints, maximizing efficiency while addressing environmental concerns and ease of operation.

Clients include homeowners and remote‑site operators who are too far from utility lines, want backup power, or wish to reduce reliance on fossil fuels.

Jon’s motivation stemmed from a desire to translate his hands‑on mechanical expertise into the renewable sector, while Holly values the independence of business ownership and helping clients build systems that work. Their involvement in community education — teaching at local colleges, exhibiting at energy fairs, and serving on the Nebraskans for Solar board — reflects a commitment to growing the regional clean‑energy knowledge base.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar photovoltaic system design", "Wind generation system design", "System installation", "Technical consulting", "Energy independence assessment", "Product selection and sales"], "industries": ["Renewable energy", "Solar power", "Wind power", "Off-grid power systems", "Backup power systems"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom system design tailored to site constraints and owner needs", "Walk\u2011in storefront for hands\u2011on product education and purchase", "Founder\u2019s 17\u2011year automotive mechanical/electrical background applied to renewable energy", "Active industry engagement: teaching, fair participation, and board leadership in state solar advocacy"], "facts_used": ["Founded spring 1999, full-time January 2005 -> /", "Founders Jon Dixon (President) and Holly Dixon (Vice-President) -> /", "Headquarters Lincoln, Nebraska -> db", "Business: design and installation of solar and wind generation systems -> /", "Storefront for product education and sales -> /", "Jon Dixon automotive repair background and renewable energy training -> /", "Holly Dixon small business background and University of Nebraska degree -> /", "Customer types: remote locations, backup power, environmental interest -> /", "Community involvement: teaching, Midwest Renewable Energy Fair, Nebraskans for Solar board -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "opened a store-front where people could learn about and purchase systems to create their own electricity", "founded_year": "1999", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='dixon-power-systems' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
