UPDATE companies SET description='The Durable Medical Equipment Re-Use Program operates from a central warehouse in Cheltenham, Maryland, under the Maryland Department of Aging. The program was established by the state to address mobility and safety needs for residents, though a specific founding year is not published. It functions as a statewide government service rather than a private enterprise, with no individual founders named.

The program collects donated durable medical equipment, sanitizes and repairs it, then redistributes it through a network of more than a dozen distribution centers across Maryland. Inventory is divided into two categories: Basic DME — including canes, crutches, walkers, rollators, shower chairs, tub transfer benches, bedside commodes, and toilet safety rails — and Complex DME — including manual and power wheelchairs, power scooters, home hospital beds, and mechanical lifts. All equipment is provided at no cost to the recipient.

The service is available to any Maryland resident with an illness, injury, or disability, regardless of age or insurance status.

The program was created to improve quality of life by helping residents stay mobile, safe, and connected in their homes and communities. It removes financial barriers by providing equipment free of charge and does not require a prescription for basic items, while complex items require input from a qualified medical professional for safety.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Medical equipment collection", "Sanitization and refurbishment", "Inventory sorting and categorization", "Basic DME processing", "Complex DME processing", "Online and paper application intake", "Appointment-based pickup scheduling", "Donation intake and screening"], "industries": ["Healthcare", "Aging services", "Disability services", "Home healthcare", "Medical equipment redistribution"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Program run by Maryland Department of Aging -> db", "Headquarters in Cheltenham, MD -> db", "Free DME for any Marylander with illness/injury/disability -> /", "Equipment collected via donation, sanitized, repaired, redistributed -> /", "Two categories: Basic DME and Complex DME with listed examples -> /", "Distribution centers in Aberdeen, Cambridge, Centreville, Cheltenham, Columbia, Elkton, Hagerstown, Odenton, Rockville, Silver Spring, Towson, Westminster, Worcester -> /", "Partner organizations: Delmarva Community Services, Queen Anne''s County Dept of Community Services, Cecil County Aging and Disability Services, Horizon Goodwill Industries, etc. -> /", "No prescription needed for basic equipment; complex requires healthcare professional -> /", "Pickup by appointment only at distribution centers -> /", "Donation acceptance and rejection lists provided -> /"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "All equipment is collected via donation and is sanitized, repaired, and redistributed to locations throughout Maryland for pickup.", "founded_y