UPDATE companies SET description='ECI Cables Inc. has operated in Sinking Spring, Pennsylvania, since 1960. The company moved into a 50,000-square-foot facility shared with sister company RLC Electronic Systems in 2011 and completed a major remodel and expansion in 2021.

The shop produces cable assemblies, wire harnesses, and equipment wiring solutions. Services include ribbon cable assembly, DIN rail assembly, electro-mechanical assembly, sensor assemblies, box builds, wire wrapping, harness braiding, and cable over-molding. Four high-speed cutting and stripping machines process wire from 0 to 30 AWG, while termination uses multiple AMP presses, Pico pneumatic crimpers, automated crimp tooling, and hundreds of calibrated hand tools. Cable identification is handled via thermal transfer printing, hot stamping, and epoxy inking. The facility also houses a Komax Alpha 530 automated wire processing system and supports in-process crimp force monitoring, hi-pot, resistance, continuity, and pull testing.

ECI serves a broad range of sectors: aerospace, automotive, agricultural, industrial, clean room, HVAC, solar, renewable energy, transportation, water treatment, automation, fire safety, security, backup power, traffic control, goods transportation, medical, portable power, audio, outdoor lighting, general lighting, data centers, and military programs requiring MIL-I-45028A compliance.

The company emphasizes technical design assistance for harness layout, materials, plating, termination methods, and current-carrying capacity. It builds to WHMA-620-A standards with a certified instructor on staff, maintains an ISO 9001-compatible quality system, holds UL508A certification, and offers government-approved source inspection. An extensive inventory of connectors, wire, sleeving, and cable enables faster turnaround than many in-house operations.', certifications=ARRAY['IPC-WHMA-620C','ISO 9001 compatible','UL508A Certified','UL (wire certification)','MIL-I-45208A','WHMA-620-A']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Ribbon cable assembly", "DIN rail assembly", "Electro-mechanical assembly", "Sensor assemblies", "Box builds", "Wire wrapping", "Harness braiding", "Cable over-molding", "Wire cutting and stripping (0-30 AWG)", "Semi-stripping", "Hot stamping on wire jacket", "Termination with AMP presses", "Termination with Pico pneumatic crimpers", "Automated crimp tooling", "Hand crimp tools (NIST-traceable calibration)", "Thermal transfer printing", "Hot stamping for cable identification", "Epoxy inking for harsh environments", "Design assistance (materials, plating, components, harness layout, termination methods)", "Incoming material inspection", "In-process crimp force monitoring (CFA)", "Hi-pot testing", "Resistance testing", "Continuity testing", "Visual inspection", "Crimp height analysis", "Pull testing", "Custom test fixtures", "Microscopic visual inspection", "Mechanical testing"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Automotive", "Agricultural", "Industrial", "Clean rooms", "HVAC", "Solar", "Renewable Energy", "Transportation", "Water treatment", "Automation", "Fire safety", "Security", "Backup power systems", "Traffic control", "Goods transportation", "Medical", "Portable power", "Audio", "Outdoor lighting", "Lighting", "Data centers", "Military"], "materials": ["Wire (0-30 AWG)", "Lugs", "Ferrules", "Splices", "Connectors", "Sleeving", "Insulation", "L