UPDATE companies SET description='EPEC Solutions, Inc. was founded in 2016 in Clayton, North Carolina, on Christian principles of prayer and servant leadership. The company''s stated purpose is to glorify God by developing employees'' skills and serving customers as good stewards while supporting communities through service and ministry funding.

The company manufactures electrical switchboards and power distribution equipment at four facilities across North America. Its product line includes modular UL 891 switchboards rated 208–800 VAC and 1,200–6,000 A, low‑voltage UL 891 switchboards (480/600/800 VAC, 400–4,000 A) with an optional 55 % domestic content, a 660–800 VAC BoS family featuring an industry‑first 800 V main breaker, unit substation skidded solutions, and 1,200–6,000 A 800 VDC switchboards for AI data centers. Additional offerings cover AC recombiners, rack‑on‑rails systems, remote power panels, PDUs, grounding transformers, integrated solar skids, and EV charging switchboards.

EPEC serves the data center, solar, battery energy storage (BESS), and EV charging sectors, primarily in the United States and Canada. Customers include renewable power plant developers and data center operators who collaborate directly with EPEC''s engineering and project management teams for tailored designs.

The company differentiates itself through pre‑fabricated factory solutions that reduce installation risk and speed deployment, compact modular designs packing up to 30 feeders in a 90″×60″×36″ footprint, electronic‑trip MCCBs to eliminate nuisance tripping, and 100 % rated breakers that allow smaller cable sizing. Its mission‑driven culture emphasizes servant leadership and community advocacy.', certifications=ARRAY['UL 891']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["UL 891 switchboard manufacturing", "Modular switchboard design and assembly", "Low-voltage switchboard production (480/600/800 VAC)", "Skidded unit substation fabrication", "Solar AC combiner manufacturing (MLO and main breaker)", "EV charging switchboard and skid production", "Power distribution unit (PDU) assembly", "Remote power panel (RPP) manufacturing", "Grounding transformer and line reactor integration", "Custom integrated skid fabrication", "Rack-on-rails system assembly", "Solar string inverter rack manufacturing", "Auxiliary power center production", "Pad-mount AC combiner manufacturing", "Rack-mount MLO AC combiner manufacturing", "Engineering consultation and project management", "Tailored design collaboration"], "industries": ["Data centers", "Solar energy", "Battery energy storage systems (BESS)", "EV charging infrastructure", "Renewable power plants"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Industry-first 800\u202fV main breaker option on BoS family switchboards", "Up to 55\u202f% domestic content available on UL 891 low\u2011voltage switchboards", "Pre\u2011fabricated skidded unit substations to reduce field installation risk and time", "Direct collaboration with in\u2011house engineering and project management teams", "Compact modular switchboards with up to 30 feeders in a 90\u2033\u00d760\u2033\u00d736\u2033 enclosure"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2016 -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Clayton, North Carolina -> db", "Manufactures UL