UPDATE companies SET description='East Jordan Plastics operates from East Jordan, Michigan, where Ken and Shirley Diller founded East Jordan Box and Crate Co. four generations ago to produce wooden greenhouse flats for Midwestern bedding-plant growers. The business remains family-owned and has served the horticulture industry exclusively for nearly 80 years, evolving from wooden flats to a full line of sustainable plastic plant containers.

The company injection-molds a comprehensive range of horticultural containers — SHUTTLE™ hanging baskets, planters and bowls; the patented SHUTTLE POT® STADIUM® pots and trays with squared-off sides for space-saving shipping; SHUTTLE POT® and SHUTTLE TRAY® lines built for quick de-nesting on automated lines; plus trays, carriers, flats, inserts, and precision-engineered plug and propagation trays. A closed-loop recycling program, certified for Post-Consumer Recycled (PCR) content by AM Testing, feeds reclaimed material back into production.

Customers are greenhouse and nursery growers, from large automated operations to smaller propagators. Bradford Greenhouses and Linwell Gardens are cited as users; the STADIUM line is noted to deliver 12–14% more growing space per bench. Trays and carriers are designed for automated destacking, filling, transplanting and transport equipment, while plug trays support both hand-sticking and high-volume seed sowing.

The company says its differentiation comes from a single-industry focus, a closed-loop sustainability model that recycles used containers into new ones, and product designs — such as the STADIUM® line’s flat sides for labeling and offset printing — that address growers’ handling, shipping and marketing needs.', certifications=ARRAY['PCR Plastic Certification (AM Testing)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection molding", "Closed-loop recycling", "Custom offset printing on containers", "Design for automated destacking, filling, transplanting and transport", "Precision engineering of plug and propagation trays"], "industries": ["Horticulture", "Greenhouse growing", "Nursery", "Bedding plant production"], "materials": ["Post-Consumer Recycled (PCR) plastic", "Plastic"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founders Ken and Shirley Diller; started as East Jordan Box and Crate Co. -> db, /", "Location East Jordan, Michigan -> db", "Family-owned (testimonial) -> /", "Nearly 80 years in horticulture -> /", "Injection-molded SHUTTLE\u2122, SHUTTLE POT\u00ae STADIUM\u00ae, SHUTTLE POT\u00ae & SHUTTLE TRAY\u00ae lines -> /", "Closed-loop recycling with PCR certification from AM Testing -> /", "Made in USA -> /", "Customers Bradford Greenhouses, Linwell Gardens -> /", "STADIUM pots provide 12-14% more space -> /", "Products for automated destacking, filling, transplanting, transport -> /", "Plug trays precision-engineered for exact tolerances -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "From those wooden flats to today''s comprehensive line of sustainable plastic plant containers, East Jordan Plastics remains committed to the only industry it has ever served \u2014 horticulture.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=