UPDATE companies SET description='Ebanista School of Fine Woodworking operates in the Georgetown neighborhood of Seattle, Washington.

The facility combines a teaching environment with a professional furniture studio. All instructors are specialists with a minimum of 45 years of professional woodworking experience. Class sizes are intentionally limited to ensure maximum individual attention. The curriculum covers the design and making of inspired furniture, providing a foundation that students can apply to cabinetmaking, instrument making, boatbuilding, fine carpentry, and other precision disciplines.

The school serves students of all ages seeking to develop professional-level woodworking skills.

Ebanista was created to fill a gap identified through years of requests for a school of this caliber. The name, Spanish for "fine woodworker," reflects a philosophy that wood''s variability makes it a uniquely expressive material. The school''s approach emphasizes deep material understanding and precision, positioning woodworking as a gateway to broader design and engineering thinking.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Furniture design instruction", "Fine woodworking instruction", "Cabinetmaking instruction", "Instrument making instruction", "Boatbuilding instruction", "Fine carpentry instruction", "Professional furniture making"], "industries": ["Education", "Furniture making", "Cabinetmaking", "Instrument making", "Boatbuilding", "Fine carpentry"], "materials": ["Wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Instructors with minimum 45 years professional woodworking experience", "Intentionally limited class sizes for maximum individual attention", "Combined school and professional furniture studio in one facility", "Curriculum focused on furniture design and making as a foundation for multiple woodworking disciplines"], "facts_used": ["Located in Georgetown area of Seattle -> /", "Classes began fall 2018 -> /", "Founded by Jonathan Cohen (implied from Google talk quote) -> /", "Instructors have minimum 45 years professional experience -> /", "School houses both a school and professional furniture studio -> /", "Class sizes intentionally limited -> /", "Curriculum covers furniture design, cabinetmaking, instrument making, boatbuilding, fine carpentry -> /", "Ebanista means ''fine woodworker'' in Spanish -> /"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "unclear", "type_evidence": "The Ebanista School of Fine Woodworking was founded to bring a school capable of offering the highest level of instruction in the design and making of inspired furniture to the Pacific Northwest.", "founded_year": "2018", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": ["English"], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ebanista-school-of-fine-woodworking' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Eben Blaney Fine Contemporary Furniture operates from a studio and showroom in Edgecomb, Maine. Founder Eben Blaney has been designing and building contemporary furniture for well over 20 years, establishing a practice centered on handmade, one-of-a-kind and limited-production pieces.

The workshop produces custom furniture commissions and a rotating line of limited-production items including tables, seating, case pieces, beds, mirrors, and decor. Each piece is built individually or in small batches using precise joinery and imaginative engineering, then signed, dated, and numbered before delivery. The work relies on carefully selected hardwoods chosen for their beauty and character.

Clients include individual collectors, design professionals, and trade buyers across the Northeast, nationally, and internationally. Pieces are sold directly through the Edgecomb showroom, via the online platform Incollect, and by commission. The company serves the residential furniture, interior design, and custom furnishings markets.

